---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const source = 'https://github.com/theelinumbriel/builtbyelisa/tree/main/tools/manual';
---

<Base title="Manual | Elisa Diop-Weyer" description="An iPad sketchbook for designing interfaces with AI.">
  <article class="manual">
    <h1 class="title">Manual</h1>
    <p class="lede">A sketchbook for building interfaces with AI.</p>
    <p>
      Sometimes drawing an interface is easier than describing it. Manual gives
      that drawing a place in the conversation: a white page on an iPad, named
      screens along the bottom, and a Save button that sends the sketch to a Mac.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sketch a first screen, save it, and ask a coding assistant to build from
      it. Then pull the working web page onto a new screen and draw the next
      changes directly over it. Each saved revision keeps its own reference image.
    </p>
    <p>
      The canvas supports Pencil input, pan and zoom, stroke erasing, undo and
      redo, notes, and screenshot imports. Devices connect over Wi-Fi through
      a private pairing link; drawings stay on the Mac.
    </p>
    <p class="source"><a href={source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source and setup instructions ↗</a></p>
    <p class="note">Manual runs locally with Node.js. Google Chrome is needed for web page capture.</p>
    <p class="back"><a href={`${base}/portfolio`}>← Portfolio</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .manual { max-width: 42rem; }
  .lede { font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .manual > p { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .source { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
